      § A410-1


General provisions.     









 A.  This table is the result of an effort to devise a systematic and preferably complete outline of the structure and functions of Town government as embodied in the General Laws of the Commonwealth, the Town Charter and other special legislation, the General Bylaws of the Town, and regulations adopted by Town boards and officials. Experience has shown that some such guide is needed for ready access to the various sources of law governing the operation of Town government. B.  Explanation of citations. All provisions cited without parentheses are those in effect as of April 1996. Provisions cited in parentheses are either those which would govern in the absence of Charter or bylaw provisions or annual statutes later incorporated into the General Laws. Statutory references are to chapters and sections of the General Laws, or to annual acts. Bylaw references are to the compilation adopted by the 1973 Annual Town Meeting or to the date of another subsequent Town Meeting vote.                  










